        <common:reviewDetails xml:lang="en">Internal reviews have been asked to review the plausibility of the unit process, LCIA scores, and DQRs. Internal reviewers have also been asked to review the data for EF compliancy. The consortium is therefore responsible for aspects such as compliancy with the ILCD format, including validation in Look@LCI, and nomenclature.
Internal reviwers have been asked to judge based on the process name, that the unit process models in a complete and representative way the  process in the requested location. The review encompassed the plausability of:
- exchanges with nature (elementary flows) as well as exchanges such as product and waste flows.
- meta information (general comment, technology comment, system boundaries, allocation, cut-off rules, etc.). Reviewers were asked to judge if the provided information is enough to understand the content of the process.
- LCIA scores
- DQRs including precision, technology, time and geography. As well as the overall DQR.</common:reviewDetails>
